    "content": "High Point University (HPU) is a private liberal arts institution in North Carolina known as \"The Premier Life Skills University,\" focusing on experiential learning, career readiness, and student success. Consistently ranked by The Princeton Review as the #1 Best-Run College, it boasts a 99% job/graduate school placement rate and offers 73 undergraduate majors. Key Details About High Point University: Academics: HPU offers 73 undergraduate majors and 70 minors, alongside various graduate programs. Key academic units include the Phillips School of Business, Congdon School of Health Sciences, and Workman School of Dental Medicine. Campus Life & Environment: Known for its \"extraordinary\" campus, HPU is ranked for having top-tier dorms and a beautiful campus environment. It is a Methodist-affiliated institution that emphasizes values-based learning. Admissions & Cost: The university is moderately competitive with a roughly 77% acceptance rate. Total estimated costs for tuition, fees, and room/board for 2026-2027 are approximately $71,429. Athletics: HPU competes in NCAA Division I athletics as part of the Big South Conference, featuring 17 varsity sports. Note: While HPU receives high accolades in publications like The Princeton Review, some forum users on Reddit note that some of their marketing and rankings can seem overwhelming to some applicants.",
